        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0111" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg765"/>

                <head>No. 360.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation, Japan</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokei</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 26,
                        1874</date>. (Received October 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 124.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 12th ultimo, Mr. Hawes, our consul
                    at Hakodadi, by a dispatch of that date, notified me that Mr. L. Haber, late
                    acting German consul at that port, had been murdered on the previous evening by
                    a Japanese. The murderer was arrested, tried, convicted, and on the 10th <pb
                        facs="0112" n="766" xml:id="pg766"/> instant executed, and a proclamation
                    was issued by the government condemning all such assassinations and manifesting
                    a determination to visit such crimes with swift punishment. A copy of the
                    proclamation is herewith inclosed.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. A. BINGHAM.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d56-a1.xml" xpointer="d56-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
